\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {15}{\ignorespaces Controlled re-scan scenarios A--D (room-scoped robot hall, 55 objects), top-down view. Colored points are the segmented clusters, thin rotated rectangles their explicit-model footprints with node names, and the dark contour the test-room boundary; each edited object is annotated with the matcher's decision. (A)~A repeat scan with no changes carries all 55 verdicts at zero VLM cost. (B)~A 3.6\,m chair move is classified \texttt  {moved} with its node ID preserved. (C)~A removed object is marked \texttt  {absent} (node kept and flagged) and a newly placed object is \texttt  {inserted} under a new ID; only the insertion is re-verified. (D)~Partial occlusion: both cropped objects still match at 20\%, but at 40\% matching fails into two false-absent plus two false-new pairs---the matcher's quantified breaking point.}}{30}{figure.caption.24}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:update}{{15}{30}{Controlled re-scan scenarios A--D (room-scoped robot hall, 55 objects), top-down view. Colored points are the segmented clusters, thin rotated rectangles their explicit-model footprints with node names, and the dark contour the test-room boundary; each edited object is annotated with the matcher's decision. (A)~A repeat scan with no changes carries all 55 verdicts at zero VLM cost. (B)~A 3.6\,m chair move is classified \texttt {moved} with its node ID preserved. (C)~A removed object is marked \texttt {absent} (node kept and flagged) and a newly placed object is \texttt {inserted} under a new ID; only the insertion is re-verified. (D)~Partial occlusion: both cropped objects still match at 20\%, but at 40\% matching fails into two false-absent plus two false-new pairs---the matcher's quantified breaking point}{figure.caption.24}{}}
